## HTTP — soft builtins

### Client
`http_get_json_i64(host, port, path, field) -> i64`

Issues HTTP/1.1 GET, parses JSON response body field (uses `json_get_i64`).

`http_post_json_i64(host, port, path, json_body, field) -> i64`

Issues HTTP/1.1 POST with `Content-Type: application/json`, parses response field.

```
let n = http_get_json_i64("127.0.0.1", 8080, "/api", "value")
let m = http_post_json_i64("127.0.0.1", 8080, "/api", "{\"n\": 7}", "value")
```

### Server (one-shot)
`http_serve_once_json_i64(port, path, value) -> i64`

Listens on `port`, accepts one connection, and if the request path matches,
responds with `{"value": <value>}` (HTTP 200). Returns `0` on path match,
`1` on path mismatch with 404 JSON, `-1` on I/O error.

`http_serve_once_echo_json_i64(port, path, field) -> i64`

Same listen/accept shape, but parses integer `field` from the request JSON body
and echoes `{"value": N}`. Returns `N` on success, `1` on path mismatch, `-1`
on error.

Pair with a fiber client (see `rt/tests/http_post_echo_smoke.c`) or an
external HTTP client.

Low-level TCP remains in `std/net.ryx` (`tcp_listen`, `tcp_connect`, …).
